        {
          "id": 1170919805,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "This change could probably have some side effects on other dissectors, anyway I guess that RDP is not the only protocol that starts with a protocol and switch to TLS after a few packets of negotiation.\n\nThe previous behavior is rather strange, with the heuristics I don't really see a case where we would identify some TLS records, late in the conversation, and that forcing SSL decoding of first packets (during the second pass) would help, because in this case I guess the heuristics would have catch that it was TLS traffic way before. If you find a TLS record only at packet 25 of the conversation, then why forcing TLS on  packets 0-24, while heuristics didn't identify them as TLS at first pass ?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5717614,
            "username": "hardening1",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "David Fort",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/5717614/avatar.png?v=1773998323",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/hardening1"
